                <pb facs="0523" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg515"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760F.62/285: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-23T11:00:00-04:00">May 23, 1938—11 a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>75. Your 260, May 21, 6 p.m. We appreciate your suggestions as to any step we
                    could take which might be useful in the present crisis but after consideration
                    have decided that for the present at least a simultaneous approach to Berlin and
                    Praha would not be advisable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
